# Linear issue naming (maintainer private tracker)

When creating or updating issues in the **private** Linear workspace via MCP or UI, follow the same EOS pattern as [GitHub Issues](https://github.com/renanflustosa/octo-cluster/issues).

## Title format (required)

```text
[domain] imperative verb + object
```

Examples: `[governance] revise README governance section`, `[eval] run TIP pilot ast-grep vs grep-first`

## Valid domain prefixes

Use exactly one domain label that matches the title prefix:

`governance` · `standards` · `dx` · `eval` · `orchestration` · `mcp` · `token` · `rag` · `context` · `memory` · `kernel` · `ci` · `security` · `docs` · `observability`

Map title-only aliases: `adapter` → `dx`, `pack` → `kernel` or `mcp` (by scope).

## Rules

- English imperative verb after the domain prefix
- Exactly **one** domain label per issue (meta labels like `ai-ready`, `Bug`, `test` are optional)
- Forbidden: Portuguese titles, vague objects (`Fix stuff`), gerunds without imperative verb, multiple domain labels

## Before marking `ai-ready`

1. Title matches `^\[[a-z]+\] [a-z].+`
2. Domain label equals title prefix
3. DoR checklist complete per [eos.md](../../docs/governance/eos.md#definition-of-ready-dor)

## Consumer boundary

Never paste Linear issue IDs, URLs, or workspace names into the **public** octo-cluster tree. Private tracker details belong in gitignored `docs/_private/` or local vault overlays only.
